{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SeparatedIndex","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SeparatedIndex","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothIndex","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SeparatedHeight"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.index_X_sq_weight_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.index_X_sq_weight_two","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedIndex.lean#L164-L173","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.index_separated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.index_separated","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedIndex.lean#L110-L151","doc":"**`index (U(x)·V(y)) = index U + index V`** for disjoint variable groups, over a domain.\n\nThe `≥` half is `index_mul_ge` plus the rename-invariance above, and holds over any\n`CommRing`.  The `≤` half is the new content and is where `IsDomain` is used: it picks\nmulti-indices realising each index and needs their combination to occur in the product, whose\ncoefficient there is a product of two non-zero elements.  See the module header — over a ring\nwith zero divisors that monomial can cancel and the inequality can be strict.\n\n`⊤` is handled by the same argument rather than by a special case: if `translate α U = 0` then\nthe left side is `⊤` and so is the right, since `⊤ + x = ⊤`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.index_rename_inr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.index_rename_inr","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedIndex.lean#L100-L106","doc":"The right-hand counterpart of `index_rename_inl`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.index_rename_inl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.index_rename_inl","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedIndex.lean#L88-L98","doc":"Injecting `U` into the larger variable set does not change its index.\n\nNow a one-line specialisation of `index_rename_of_injective` in `RothIndex.lean`.  An earlier\nversion of this module proved it directly; deriving it instead is the check that the general\ntransport lemma really does subsume the injection-specific ones. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.idxWeight_sumElim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.idxWeight_sumElim","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedIndex.lean#L75-L84","doc":"**`idxWeight` is additive on `Finsupp.sumElim`.**  The support of `sumElim i j` is the\ndisjoint sum of the two supports, so the defining sum splits with no overlap — this is the\ncombinatorial reason the index is *exactly* additive rather than merely superadditive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.translate_rename_inr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.translate_rename_inr","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedIndex.lean#L61-L71","doc":"The right-hand counterpart of `translate_rename_inl`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.translate_rename_inl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.translate_rename_inl","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SeparatedIndex.lean#L48-L59","doc":"Translating by `Sum.elim α β` and injecting on the left is injecting and translating by\n`α`: the `β` half never sees a variable of `U`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}